    "description": "Allocation of land plots from Regional Industrial Estates to set up new Industries",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13402",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-09-08 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The selection of investors for investment in Industrial Estates is carried out by the \"Regional Industrial Service Committee\" established in accordance with the provisions of the Industrial Promotion Act, No.46 of 1990 and the \"Project Evaluation Committee of the Ministry\" appointed by the Secretary to the Ministry. Accordingly, the Project Evaluation Committee of the Ministry has recommended the allocation of land plots as well, for 38 investment projects from among the 42 project proposals recommended by the Regional Industrial Service Committees. The total value of investments to be made by the said 38 investors is Rs.2,548.22 million, and it is also expected to generate about 1,559 direct employment opportunities through those industrial projects. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Industry and Entrepreneurship Development to provide land plots from the relevant industrial estates on lease basis for a maximum period of 35 years to the said investors, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2025-09-08-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2025-09-08",
    "description": "Ensuring the Sustainable Operation of Cascade System",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13401",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-09-08 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- A group of interconnected tanks that exist within small and medium catchment areas in the dry zone of Sri Lanka is known as a Cascade System. The Cascade System, a masterpiece of Sri Lanka's irrigation civilization, has been designated a World Heritage by the Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations (FAO) and the United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization (UNESCO). Protecting the Cascade Systems, developing them with a sustainable plan, and working to bring its benefits to society have been identified as a task that must be carried out at present. The Department of Agrarian Development has issued Circular No.06/2023 regarding the establishment of \"Cascade System Management Committees\" to facilitate the active participation of farmers and other stakeholders involved in economic activities related to these Cascade Systems, which protect social, economic and environmental balance, and to manage those systems while preserving them. The proposal made by the Minister of Agriculture, Livestock, Land and Irrigation to issue a new Circular jointly by the Ministry of Agriculture, Livestock, Land and Irrigation and the Ministry of Public Administration, Provincial Councils and Local Government, enabling to establish Cascade System Management Committees, to implement the Cascade System Management Plan and to further regularize\u00a0 the implementation of the relevant Committee process at district and divisional level, by amending the aforesaid Circular instructions as appropriate, and to take action to introduce amendments to the Agrarian Development Act No. 46 of 2000 to legalize the provisions of the said Circular, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
